1) Load Image and AI Network
The code loads the input image and prepares it for analysis.
It also loads the pretrained SqueezeNet neural network which is used for image classification.

2) Traditional Method (Color Segmentation using K-Means)
The code converts the image into LAB colour space and uses K-means clustering to group pixels with similar colours.
One of the clusters is selected to create a mask that separates the target colour region from the rest of the image.

3) AI Method (Image Classification)
The code uses SqueezeNet to analyse the image and predict its most likely category displaying the predicted label and confidence score.

4) Results Analysis
The code displays and compares the K-means segmentation result with the AI classification result.
K-means identifies regions based on colour similarity, while SqueezeNet recognises objects based on features learned during training.
